      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "At the beginning, if we can capture data from FMA, we should continue the process."
      ],
      "reason": "Both carry the payload \"No continue\", which directly contradicts the explicit source instruction to \"continue the process\" after either data capture attempt."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if we can capture data from Jamendo, we should continue the process."
      ],
      "reason": "Both carry the payload \"No continue\", which directly contradicts the explicit source instruction to \"continue the process\" after either data capture attempt."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b5->n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the sample is missing, we should continue the process. We should download the sample."
      ],
      "reason": "The guard directs the \"Yes\" path (sample is missing) straight to the download action. This reverses the expected condition-to-outcome mapping, as downloading logically applies when the sample is present, not missing."
    }
  ],
  "omissions": [
